Append to CommentsAppleScript for iTunes, in Mac OS X or OS 9Find more free AppleScriptsand info on writing your ownat Doug's AppleScriptshttp://www.malcolmadams.com/itunes/Currently if you edit the comments of multiple tracks, iTunes will delete any text that may have been there before. This script lets you append text to multiple tracks' comments without losing the current comment text.Place this script in iTunes "Scripts" folder (see accompanying "Install" clipping). Select some tracks to edit and run the script from iTunes Scripts Menu.If no tracks are selected, the script will assume all the tracks in the selected Playlist are to be edited.Enter some new text in the dialog that appears.Next select to append the new text Before or After current comments.The script will alert you when it is finished. It won't take long.* You can edit the script to change the "separator", the bit of text that goes between the new and current comment text. Currently this is set to a single space. Open the script in Script Editor and read the commented instructions.My name in Doug Adamsdougadams@mac.com